   "number": "5.1",
   "title": "Heather Majaury, Kitchener",
   "closed": false,
   "video_start": 182.209,
   "video_end": 405.695,
   "notes": [
    "<p>Heather Majaury provided a delegation on the encampment evictions at Soper Park in Cambridge, Ontario. They expressed concerns about the referenced evictions, specifically, the approach taken by municipal officials to remove the individuals from the encampment. They further expressed the importance of supporting individuals suffering from homelessness in order to assist them in accessing adequate housing. H. Majaury also noted that Municipalities need to meaningfully engage individuals to identify alternative places to live that are acceptable to them.</p>\n<p>A copy of her speaking notes, biography, and a link to the referenced video is attached to the original minutes.</p>"
   ],
